From dc76c40e4c03677b07fef1044cbc767f659d91b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:44:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(trace): even-width Centerline strokes trace on their
 centre (ADR-394)

A stroke an even number of pixels wide has its centre between two pixel
centres, and the skeleton keeps whole pixels, so Centerline traced such
strokes half a pixel to one side. Each traced point on a pixel centre now
moves to the ridge of the distance field, read one pixel to either side
across the stroke, by at most half a pixel. Junctions stay where they are.

Two changes come with it, because centring exposed them:
- The tip walk that runs a stroke out to the end of its ink read the
  ridge from the nearest pixel, which turned the walk 22.5 degrees off a
  round cap's axis. It now reads between pixel centres. Without this,
  centring pushed the regression bar's 9 px arc to 1.25 px, over its
  1 px limit.
- After rebuilding a corner, the sharpener could build a second one
  beside it from the next point's window. Centred legs pass the gates more
  often, and on a 12 px stroke's 45 degree corners the second corner stood
  1.5-1.8 px off the pen's path. Centreline strokes now skip a candidate
  whose window or tangent chords take in a corner already rebuilt. The
  contour tracer does not ask for this rule, so outlines are unchanged.

Measured against the previous commit with the audit's centreline bench:
- 21-stroke corpus: mean distance from the true centre 0.250 -> 0.102 px,
  mean 95th percentile 0.39 -> 0.20 px; coverage stays 100% and fragment
  counts are unchanged. Every stroke holds or improves its mean except the
  4 px X (0.093 -> 0.186 px): one tip ends 0.71 px off its axis instead of
  1.28 px, and the output spline shared with the contour tracer bows the
  248 px chord next to it by up to its 0.45 px cap.
- The 8 px corner and tee: largest deviation 4.03 -> 4.00 px, exactly the
  half stroke width the traced line runs past the true centreline's end.
- In-repo regression bar: largest deviation 0.69 -> 0.19 px for h-stroke,
  l-corner and cross; the arc 0.79 -> 0.10 px.
- 290 synthetic bends: mean local error 0.85 -> 0.57 px. 209 improve by
  more than 0.1 px and 28 get worse, by at most 0.79 px, 21 of them at
  3-6 px widths. The one-corner rule alone changes five bends, all for
  the better (the 12 px 45 degree corners to 0.6-0.7 px).
- Contour presets: identical output, timing aside, on the 48 audit corpus
  traces and the 8 traces of the dragon and logo.
- Dragon: 2,518 -> 2,522 paths, 67,610 -> 65,986 vertices; share of traced
  length on ink 0.822 -> 0.835. Logo: 74 paths, 2,588 -> 2,665 vertices;
  traced radius relative to the local ridge 0.909 -> 0.917. On the two
  images the one-corner rule leaves out 36 of 752 rebuilt corners.
  Centring costs about 68 ms on the dragon's 98,000 chain points.

